  "Description": {
    "Cost": 6191331,
    "Rarity": 2,
    "UIName": "Skinwalker II",
    "Id": "chassisdef_skinwalker_II_SKW-2-MSTAKE",
    "Name": "Skinwalker II",
    "Details": "This Skinwalker II was assigned to legendary mercenary Nikki \"Ms. Take,\" whose exceptional record and reliability convinced the Society to offer them a permanent contract. Despite their unconventional methods and infamous enthusiasm for nuclear weaponry, the Society entrusted Ms. Take with an iATM-12 supplied with experimental Fusion ammunition, supported by a Society Streak NARC for precise delivery. Twin Tesla Rifles provide defensive electronic disruption, while Nova CEWS integrates the mercenary with Society formations. Most unusual is a compact Fission Reactor installed alongside the experimental ammunition. More than a power source, the reactor serves as a deliberate failsafe, ensuring neither the Fusion ammunition nor its technology can survive the 'Mech's capture. Given the pilot chosen to operate it, the Society apparently had little concern that the failsafe would go unused if necessary.\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Quirk: Stable</color></b>\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Drop Cost Multiplier: 1.08</color></b>\n\n<color=#FFEF00>Arm Actuator Limits: Omni</color>",
    "Icon": "Skinwalkerii"
  },
  "VariantName": "SKW-2-MSTAKE",
  "ChassisTags": {
    "items": [
      "ArmLimitUpperLeft",
      "ArmLimitUpperRight",
      "OmniMech",
      "SocietyMech"
    ]
  },
  "StockRole": "Fast Striker",
  "YangsThoughts": "Oh, I've heard of this mercenary, Boss. Legendary career, never leaves a contract unfinished, and apparently never met a nuclear weapon they didn't like. The Society gave them experimental Fusion ammunition, a Streak NARC to put it exactly where they want it, and a pair of Tesla Rifles to make shooting back considerably harder. Then they installed a Fission Reactor to destroy the whole package before capture. That's either an incredible amount of trust or the worst case of enabling I've ever seen.",
